## Context

Arena run 2026-10-29, one Opus team lead, 6 merges, 1.33 of 5 USD, zero stalls, zero leftover trees; what nearly failed was agent context (213K and 192K of about 236K).

## Scope

skills/raid/references/autonomous-brief.md, cited from raid SKILL.md and agents/team-lead.md, holding only what no existing reference covers:

1. a hard USD cap that includes child spend, with a ledger line per wave showing the arithmetic (spent so far + estimate of in-flight = projected);
2. the author's by-right decisions queued, one line each with a default and a price, delivered in the final report;
3. a context rule: at about 75% of the ceiling (rules/guards.md), write a handoff note on the branch and hand bounded risky windows to a fresh agent;
4. a broadcast to every live agent before taking a shared resource (GPU, production), where the runtime offers one; otherwise a line in the raid log.

Existing homes are cited, not restated: watchdogs (circuit-breakers.md), sitreps from side effects (sitrep.md), verbatim-retry ban (merge-permission-denial.md), advisor model (workflow § Escalation).

rules/claude-code.md § Allow rules gains one sentence: a classifier denial is rewritten to match an allow rule literally (git -C, no cd prefix) or logged and skipped, never retried verbatim.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The reference exists and is cited by raid SKILL.md and agents/team-lead.md.
- [ ] Each of its four items is absent from the other raid references (grep in the PR).
- [ ] The denial sentence is in rules/claude-code.md § Allow rules.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
